From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: correct msgbox bank and watchdog IRQs

Adapt well0nez's 0024d to our tree: stock msgbox bank order is SPI
46/109/108. SPI 21 was unrelated to the ARM inbox; old storm observations
using that mapping do not qualify the actual bank-0 IRQ. The watchdog is
SPI 53, avoiding its erroneous overlap with msgbox bank 0.

Keep the single 0x1000 register window. Our driver already requests only
index 0; preserve that ownership rather than claiming ARISC/MIPS lines.
Unlike the source patch, avoid assigning S/PDIF ownership to SPI 21: our
saved stock DT gives OWA0 SPI 23.

Link: https://github.com/well0nez/allwinner-h713-linux/blob/149f51d0df24c45b12674c81aab128b1fc8f5d4b/mainline/patches/kernel/0024d-arm64-dts-h713-msgbox-three-lines-watchdog-spi-53.patch
Link: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/issues/4

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1538,7 +1538,7 @@
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-wdt",
 				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
 			reg = <0x02051000 0x20>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 46 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 53 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			clocks = <&osc24M>;
 		};
 
@@ -1947,7 +1947,12 @@
 		cpu_comm: cpu-comm@3003000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-cpu-comm";
 			reg = <0x03003000 0x1000>;
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 21 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			/* Stock bank order: ARM inbox, ARISC inbox, MIPS inbox.
+			 * CPU_COMM owns only bank 0; do not request the other lines.
+			 */
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 46 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 109 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 108 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_MSGBOX>;
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_MSGBOX>;
 			shared-memory = <&cpu_comm_reserved>;
